 # Packing
 
+## Mac game actions
+
+### In-game menus use the launcher's choices and committed saves
+
+- **Symptom:** a Mac app offers Console mode before Play, but no Docked/Handheld switch while the game runs. The earlier menu contribution in [PR #104](https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/pull/104) also predates the shared launcher, save paths and transactional saves.
+- **Cause:** startup settings belong to the launcher and its validated per-game store; the running host owns operation mode, audio and committed saves. A separate menu preference store or an archive restored over an active guest would disagree with those owners.
+- **Fix:** the native menus from [PR #921](https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/pull/921) use `launcher.json` for offered console-mode, frame-rate and render-scale choices, the existing preference keys, default removal and launch-override precedence. Mode changes use `dm_set_opmode`; supported frame-rate/render-scale changes update the runtime page atomically. Volume and mute preserve audio consumption and lifecycle suspension. Screenshots use NVN's existing queue. Manual backup export clones committed normal/device saves into the checked `.dmsync` format; restore validates a staged copy, waits for the host to exit, retains a recovery copy and coordinates the existing save-folder lease and cloud synchronization. The game and startup windows disable automatic tabbing.
+- **Found on:** [Metroid Dread](../../dm/games/010093801237C000/README.md#found-on-this-game), whose opening/title menu checks were reported by PR #921's author. That report is not a new gameplay check of this integration.
+
 ## Game packages
 
